 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "A volcano on the other side of the world may have put a German on the first bicycle.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 124
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "April, eighteen fifteen. Mount Tambora in Indonesia exploded, the most powerful eruption in recorded history.",
   "from": 128,
   "to": 303
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Its sulphur veiled the sky, and the whole planet cooled.",
   "from": 307,
   "to": 400
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In Europe, eighteen sixteen became the year without a summer. Cold rain rotted the harvests.",
   "from": 404,
   "to": 536
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "But oats grew scarce and costly, and many could no longer feed their horses.",
   "from": 539,
   "to": 649
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "farmer",
   "text": "Not a single oat left!",
   "from": 653,
   "to": 689
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Many horses starved, or were slaughtered for meat and hides. Without a horse, every trip to town meant walking.",
   "from": 692,
   "to": 842
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In Mannheim, an inventor named Karl Drais dreamed up a horse that never eats.",
   "from": 846,
   "to": 965
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "So he built one out of wood. But where did the legs go?",
   "from": 969,
   "to": 1060
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You see, his running machine had two wooden wheels in a line, a seat, and a handlebar to steer.",
   "from": 1075,
   "to": 1196
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "There were no pedals at all. You pushed off the ground with your feet, then glided.",
   "from": 1200,
   "to": 1303
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "On June twelfth, eighteen seventeen, he rode it to a coaching inn and back in about an hour.",
   "from": 1307,
   "to": 1458
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "One historian argues the starving horses inspired him, though nobody can prove it.",
   "from": 1461,
   "to": 1577
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Pedals came decades later. Every bike you ride began as a wooden horse that never needed oats.",
   "from": 1580,
   "to": 1729
  }
 ],
